# Dumps never belong in the repository.
#
# data.sql carries real accounts — auth.users rows, identities, whatever a
# learner has saved. schema.sql is harmless but large and regenerated on
# demand. Neither is source, and one of them is personal data.
#
# This file exists because an empty roles.sql once reached a commit: a smoke
# test of the export script created the directory, and the next `git add -A`
# swept it up. The file was zero bytes and the repo was unharmed, but the
# same path with a real dump in it would have published accounts.
dump/
